Function strings allow you to do neat things.
Like bold your text.../BLD
Or clear the terminal./CLRB
Function strings use a slash (/) followed by one to five characters./CONT/NOBR
They will be found and removed from anywhere in the line.
Currently implemented- CLRA, CLRB, BLD, RED, YLW, GRN, BLU, CONT, NOBR, ESC, ESCSTR/CLRB
CLRA clears the terminal after the line is displayed.
CLRB clears the terminal before the line is displayed.
BLD renders the text as bold.
RED, GRN, YLW, and BLU change the text color
CONT makes the text continue without waiting for input.
NOBR removes the full line between text.
ESC makes the line ignore comments.
ESCSTRS makes the line ignore all of these neat functions.
